---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Navbar from '../components/Navbar.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

const pillars = [
  {
    id: 'single-target',
    number: '01',
    title: 'Extreme Hardware Specialization',
    subtitle: 'Refusing generalization to extract 100% of physical silicon limits',
    content: [
      'Most machine learning inference engines attempt to be universal: supporting NVIDIA CUDA, Apple Metal, Intel oneAPI, and generic CPU fallback paths within a single codebase. While broad compatibility has utility, it introduces unavoidable compromises: leaky runtime abstractions, indirect kernel dispatch tables, excessive branching, and memory layouts dictated by the lowest common denominator.',
      'gufo takes the opposite stance: Linux x86-64 on AMD Strix Halo (RDNA 3.5 gfx1151 GPU and XDNA2 NPU) is the only planned production target. Windows, macOS, and CUDA are explicitly out of scope.',
      'By focusing 100% of engineering effort on one monolithic APU architecture, we can schedule memory access down to the exact 256-bit channel interleaving of LPDDR5X, tune SIMD vector registers to Wave32 warps, and eliminate PCIe host-staging overhead entirely.'
    ]
  },
  {
    id: 'unified-memory',
    number: '02',
    title: 'Unified Memory First',
    subtitle: 'Why unified APU architecture represents the future of personal AI',
    content: [
      'Discrete graphics cards are physically constrained by the narrow PCIe interface connecting CPU system memory to onboard VRAM. For modern multi-gigabyte open-weight models, this architecture imposes heavy staging buffer penalties, fragmentation, and severe limits on context depth.',
      'Strix Halo unifies up to 128 GiB of high-speed LPDDR5X memory across the CPU, GPU, and NPU. In gufo, weights and KV caches are mapped directly into pinned HSA virtual address descriptors with zero intermediate host copies.',
      'This architectural reality allows dense 27B parameters, 80 GiB Mixture of Experts (MoE) graphs, streaming TTS decoders, and multimodal diffusion models to run side-by-side with near-zero latency overhead.'
    ]
  },
  {
    id: 'model-owned',
    number: '03',
    title: 'Model-Owned Architectures',
    subtitle: 'Handcrafted, isolated compute graphs over generic operator runtimes',
    content: [
      'In conventional frameworks, new models are forced into standardized operator abstractions (e.g. generic MatMul, standard RMSNorm). When models employ non-standard sparse routing, specialized quantization formats, or multimodal attention schedules, generic frameworks incur significant overhead.',
      'In gufo, each supported model family owns its execution pipeline under src/models/. DeepSeek V4 Flash MoE does not share mutable state or operator code with dense Qwen models; Qwen3-TTS implements its own float32 RVQ audio decoder; MiniMax-H3 manages its own diffusion transformer spatial-temporal graph.',
      'We prioritize curated excellence over quantity: we support only the highest-quality open-weight models that run comfortably within 128 GiB unified memory, and optimize each to the metal.'
    ]
  },
  {
    id: 'evidence-gated',
    number: '04',
    title: 'Evidence-Gated Performance Engineering',
    subtitle: 'Never trust vendor spec-sheets; celebrate rejection with empirical proof',
    content: [
      'Every kernel optimization and scheduling change in gufo is evaluated against empirical roofline ceilings measured directly on silicon (tools/bench/gfx1151_peak.hip) under real thermal and power limits.',
      'We operate on a strict evidence-gating policy: an optimization card is completed either by proving sustained throughput/latency gains on hardware or by rejecting the change with verified profiler traces (tools/prof/prof.py). Rejection with evidence is considered a successful engineering outcome.',
      'Crucially, performance is never accepted at the cost of correctness. Every microbenchmark and model route incorporates frozen quality oracles and bit-exact validation gates (such as --validate-hrx 1 and CTest cpu-sanitizer / gpu-full passes).'
    ]
  },
  {
    id: 'nix-and-ux',
    number: '05',
    title: 'Hermetic Reproducibility & Accessible UX',
    subtitle: 'Nix-first development integrity paired with effortless container toolboxes',
    content: [
      'Software rot and driver drift are rampant in GPU development. In gufo, direct host builds are unsupported; all builds, test presets, and PR validation gates are evaluated hermetically via Nix Flakes.',
      'However, Nix purity for developers does not mean friction for users. Through the companion gufo-org/toolboxes project, four pre-built OCI images cover serving (gufo-runtime), development (gufo-dev), evaluation against an endpoint you choose (eval-agent), and a self-contained Gufo-plus-evaluator workflow (gufo-eval-agent).',
      'We maintain strict licensing and boundary separation: clean-room implementations, complete adherence to model vendor community licenses, and zero distribution of proprietary weights.'
    ]
  }
];
---

<Layout title="Project Philosophy — gufo">
  <Navbar currentPath="/philosophy" />

  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-8">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-8">
      <!-- Left Sidebar (Docusaurus Philosophy Sidebar) -->
      <aside class="lg:col-span-1 border-r border-[#3e4042]/50 pr-4 space-y-6 text-sm">
        <div>
          <div class="font-bold text-white uppercase text-xs tracking-wider mb-2 text-slate-400">
            Core Philosophy
          </div>
          <ul class="space-y-1">
            {pillars.map((p) => (
              <li>
                <a
                  href={`#${p.id}`}
                  class="block px-2.5 py-1.5 rounded text-slate-300 hover:text-[#25c2a0] hover:bg-[#242526] transition-colors"
                >
                  {p.number}. {p.title}
                </a>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="p-3.5 bg-[#242526] rounded-lg border border-[#3e4042] text-xs space-y-2">
          <div class="text-white font-bold font-mono">The Gufo Invariant</div>
          <p class="text-slate-400 text-[11px] leading-relaxed font-sans">
            "Optimize for hardware reality, not framework abstractions. Prove gains against physical rooflines, never spec-sheets."
          </p>
        </div>
      </aside>

      <!-- Main Philosophy Content -->
      <main class="lg:col-span-3 space-y-12">
        <!-- Breadcrumbs -->
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs text-slate-400">
          <a href="/" class="hover:text-white">Home</a>
          <span>/</span>
          <span class="text-slate-200">About</span>
          <span>/</span>
          <span class="text-[#25c2a0] font-semibold">Engineering Philosophy</span>
        </div>

        <!-- Header -->
        <div class="border-b border-[#3e4042]/50 pb-8 space-y-3">
          <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-white tracking-tight">
            Engineering Philosophy &amp; Principles
          </h1>
          <p class="text-base text-slate-300 leading-relaxed max-w-3xl">
            Why gufo exists, the architectural principles behind our design decisions, and how evidence-gated development shapes our runtime.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Pillars -->
        <div class="space-y-12">
          {pillars.map((p) => (
            <section id={p.id} class="space-y-4 border-b border-[#3e4042]/50 pb-10">
              <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
                <span class="text-xs font-mono font-bold px-2 py-1 rounded bg-[#25c2a0]/10 text-[#25c2a0] border border-[#25c2a0]/30">
                  SECTION {p.number}
                </span>
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight">{p.title}</h2>
              </div>
              <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-slate-300 italic">{p.subtitle}</p>

              <div class="space-y-3 text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed font-sans">
                {p.content.map((paragraph) => (
                  <p>{paragraph}</p>
                ))}
              </div>
            </section>
          ))}
        </div>

        <!-- Callout Banner -->
        <div class="admonition admonition-tip">
          <div class="admonition-title">
            <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M13 10V3L4 14h7v7l9-11h-7z" />
            </svg>
            <span>Summary: The Gufo Engineering Contract</span>
          </div>
          <ul class="text-xs text-slate-300 space-y-1.5 list-disc list-inside mt-2">
            <li><b>Single Platform:</b> AMD Strix Halo (<code class="text-[#25c2a0] font-mono">gfx1151</code> + <code class="text-[#25c2a0] font-mono">XDNA2</code>) on Linux x86-64.</li>
            <li><b>Model Curation:</b> Only the best open weights; each model owns its isolated compute graph.</li>
            <li><b>Empirical Rooflines:</b> Verify against measured silicon ceilings, celebrate evidence-based rejection.</li>
            <li><b>Nix Purity + Container UX:</b> 100% reproducible derivations with Docker/Podman/Toolbx accessibility.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </main>
    </div>
  </div>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
